1. We chose to pass the value returned by gameObject() as a parameter to the constructor of BasicCollisionStrategy.
pros : simpler code, no extra public methods, direct removal of bricks by the strategy
cons : the instance of gameObject() allows the strategy to access all objects in the game, which has a potential
       to cause harm if misused by the strategy.

2. We added a class that holds the value of lives remaining, and 2 more subclasses of GameObject that represents
the numeric and graphic representation of the lives remaining. Each is responsible to display its own representation.

3. we added a factory class that is responsible to create random strategy according to the instructions.
Each strategy is represented by a class that implements the CollisionStrategy interface.
All behaviors are implemented mainly in the onCollision() method, but each has distinct fields and methods to operate.
Explosion - remove the brick and play the explosion sound, uses activateCollision() method of neighbor bricks to remove
the neighbors.
ExtraLife - gets the parameters needed to create a heart object in the constructor, then remove the brick and create
the heart according to the instructions
ExtraPaddle - remove the brick and create an extra paddle. We added an ExtraPaddle subclass of Paddle with distinct
behavior to achieve the correct behavior.
Puck - remove the brick and create 2 Pucks with random directions. we added Puck subclass of Ball with distinct
behavior to achieve the correct behavior.

4. The double behavior is represented bt the DoubleCollisionStrategy class which receives an array of strategies.
Upon collision, it executes all the strategies 1 by 1, adding the brick back into the game to prevent collision with
a removed object. When all strategies are done being executed, removes the brick permanently.
We used an array to allow the option of secondary double behavior. The array is created in the factory, which restricts
the maximum number of behaviors to 3.

5. We added public methods activateCollision(), addNeighbor(), getNeighborBricks(), to the Brick class in order to
implement the explosion strategy.
We also added class for each collision strategy, and for the factory.
And all the classes mentioned above.